m/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-18T22:25:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-18T22:25:00Z","body":"I wonder how easily we could get `methods.py` out of the top-level as well. It might be feasible to do such a migration via that `godot-cpp` implementation, but I'll need to play around with it. Hell, we could arguably drop `version.py` outright by putting version data in a custom `pyproject.toml` section, but that's certainly beyond the scope of this PR.\r\n\r\nI like the idea, but I'm torn on if we should do a half-measure. Would like to at least figure out why Ruff suddenly freaks out with imports","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4274677529/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4275966861","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118699#issuecomment-4275966861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118699","id":4275966861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-3hON","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-19T13:08:20Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T13:08:20Z","body":"I wouldn't consider this a half-measure, it's consolidating the current status quo that helper or build scripts should be located where they're used. This moves the `platform_methods.py` to `platform` and GLSL shader generators to their respective drivers.\r\n\r\n`methods.py` is special as it's used by most of the codebase, and so it seems fine to me that it's in the top-most level. It's the only location that's an \"ancestor\" to all the other further nested scripts.\r\n\r\nLikewise, `version.py` is the key location where we define what impacts all the codebase. It could be in `core` but it would just hide one of the most important files of the repo IMO which is well-suited at the top-level.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4275966861/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]